  <p>The "AI supervision ability" row is particularly important and under-discussed. As arXiv:2601.20245 notes, novice workers heavily relying on AI "may undermine their ability to later supervise AI effectively." If you can't read code confidently, you can't catch the errors AI makes. And AI <em>does</em> make errors — sometimes subtle, sometimes security-critical.</p>

  <div class="callout callout-amber">
    <span class="callout-label">Comprehension Debt</span>
    arXiv:2512.08942 coined "comprehension debt" — distinct from technical debt. You end up owning systems more sophisticated than your skill level can maintain. The system works, the deadline was hit, but nobody on the team fully understands why the distributed lock logic works, or what happens when the Redis connection drops.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── §03 ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="s-patterns" data-code="patterns">
  <div class="section-no">03 — Six Interaction Patterns</div>
  <h2>The How Matters More Than the What</h2>

  <p>Research from arXiv:2601.20245 identifies six distinct ways developers interact with AI coding tools. The crucial finding: three patterns that involve <em>active cognitive engagement</em> preserve learning outcomes even with heavy AI use. Three patterns that offload cognition compromise skill acquisition.</p>

  <p>The difference isn't about the quality of code produced — both groups got working code. The difference is what happens in your brain while you use the tool.</p>

  <div class="pattern-group-label pgl-good">✓ Cognitively engaged — preserves learning</div>
  <div class="pattern-grid">
    <div class="pattern-card pg-good">
      <div class="pc-icon">🎯</div>
      <div class="pc-title">Guided Generation</div>
      <div class="pc-desc">You specify the approach and constraints. AI fills in the implementation. You read each suggestion, modify it, and ask "why does this work?" before accepting.</div>
      <div class="pc-tag">↑ understanding preserved</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pattern-card pg-good">
      <div class="pc-icon">🔍</div>
      <div class="pc-title">Socratic Debugging</div>
      <div class="pc-desc">When something breaks, you describe symptoms to AI and use it to generate hypotheses. You then test each hypothesis yourself and verify the root cause before applying a fix.</div>
      <div class="pc-tag">↑ debugging skills reinforced</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pattern-card pg-good">
      <div class="pc-icon">📚</div>
      <div class="pc-title">Concept Exploration</div>
      <div class="pc-desc">Use AI as an interactive textbook. Ask it to explain a pattern multiple ways, generate examples, and quiz you on edge cases. You're building a mental model, not just getting code.</div>
      <div class="pc-tag">↑ conceptual depth grows</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="pattern-group-label pgl-bad">✗ Passively delegating — erodes skills</div>
  <div class="pattern-grid">
    <div class="pattern-card pg-bad">
      <div class="pc-icon">📋</div>
      <div class="pc-title">Copy-Paste Acceptance</div>
      <div class="pc-desc">Accept AI suggestions without reading them carefully. Tab-complete through an entire function. The code works, so you move on. You have no idea how the async error handling works.</div>
      <div class="pc-tag">↓ understanding atrophies</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pattern-card pg-bad">
      <div class="pc-icon">🔧</div>
      <div class="pc-title">Symptom-Driven Patching</div>
      <div class="pc-desc">Copy an error message into the chat. Apply whatever fix comes back. The error goes away. But you don't know <em>why</em> it went away, so the next similar error takes equally long.</div>
      <div class="pc-tag">↓ debugging skill stagnates</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pattern-card pg-bad">
      <div class="pc-icon">🏗️</div>
      <div class="pc-title">Template Harvesting</div>
      <div class="pc-desc">Build entire features from AI-generated templates without reading them. Ship the auth flow, the payment integration, the real-time websocket layer. It all works — until it doesn't.</div>
      <div class="pc-tag">↓ comprehension debt accumulates</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>You're likely doing some of each. The goal isn't to eliminate AI assistance — it's to notice when you're in a passive mode and deliberately switch to an engaged mode. The next section explains which mode to use when.</p>
</section>

<!-- ── §04 ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
